  "meta": {
    "probe": "xerox-zine-b",
    "target": "same target as xerox-zine, opposite construction: a full-bleed black handbill with everything reversed out of the toner, rather than black marks on white paper",
    "method": "the same handbill as examples/probes/xerox-zine-b.json, re-authored against default-v1. The two `cover` bites become torn fragments -- on a full-bleed plate `paper` and the ground are the same colour, so a torn fragment in paper is a real knockout with a real deckle. The four repeats of bars that stood in for body copy become six actual text ops in a monospace face, wrapped on `maxWidth`. The 150 dropout flecks are deleted and `generation` produces the dropout by re-cutting a blurred copy. One new node: a screen-blended wash that punches a light leak through the plate.",
    "v0": "xerox-zine-b, profile default-v0, pack core"
  },
  "root": {
    "id": "root",
    "type": "group",
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "stock",
        "type": "op",
        "op": "wash",
        "rngKey": "xzb/stock",
        "label": "kept from v0. It only ever showed in the 32px margin, and after `generation` that margin and the bare ground are one tone",
        "args": {
          "region": { "type": "rect", "x": -20, "y": -20, "w": 840, "h": 1240 },
          "style": { "kind": "wash", "color": "grey", "opacity": 30, "bleed": 0.2, "texture": [0.6, 0.35] }
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "plate",
        "type": "op",
        "op": "paint",
        "rngKey": "xzb/plate",
        "label": "the whole handbill is toner; the paper only shows where something is cut out of it",
        "args": {
          "region": { "type": "rect", "x": 32, "y": 32, "w": 736, "h": 1136 },
          "style": { "kind": "solid", "color": "toner", "opacity": 255 }
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "bite-top",
        "type": "op",
        "op": "fragment",
        "rngKey": "xzb/bite-top",
        "label": "a torn corner. Was a 10-point cover polygon; now a torn fragment, and it is still a real knockout because the ground and the paper colour are the same hex",
        "args": {
          "name": "arch.column",
          "x": 150,
          "y": 10,
          "span": 300,
          "rotate": 90,
          "tear": { "roughness": 0.85, "segment": 14 },
